Welcome to Voyager V3 3.5, a restoration of VaporWare's Voyager V3
for classic 68k Amiga.

Oliver Wagner started Voyager in 1995. David Gerber co-developed
it with him. The last boxed commercial product was Voyager 3.2
(16.4.2000). A limited 3.3 alpha / public-beta line followed
(from August 2000): new layout engine and window framework,
vertical nav panel, optional TearOff, CManager aliases in the
URL gadget, ftp. auto-prefix, HTML on HTTP 4xx/5xx, AS225
removed. Public betas 3.3.65 and 3.3.75; 3.3.126 (27.12.2002)
for 68k and MorphOS, followed with alpha releases. A short 3.4 CVS series
followed. Source to a 3.4 release was later published under 
the GNU GPL. This 3.5.3 build is that GPL tree made usable.

Requirements: MUI 3.8. A TCP/IP stack (bsdsocket.library).
HTTPS uses AmiSSL when amisslmaster.library can open AmiSSL 5.27,
or the included amitls.library otherwise. cybergraphics.library is 
used when availablerModeID). 

This Free and Open Source release does not need
vapor_toolkit.library or a keyfile.


See Docs/Readme.Docs and Docs/voyager3docs/main.html in this
drawer (factory fastlink Docs). README.md / CHANGELOG.md are
in the source tree:

  https://github.com/amigazen/Voyager
  http://www.amigazen.com/voyager/
  voyager@amigazen.com

------------------------------------------------------------

Newsflash: New in Voyager V3 3.5

* HTTPS connections load using either AmiSSL (if installed) or
  AmiTLS (included in the release package).

* Printing functionality has been completed: Print dialog, menu,
  toolbar, and ARexx Print ASK; text to PRT:; graphical
  printer.device bands; TurboPrint when Turboprint: is assigned.

* UTF-8 HTML, from the MIME charset or a META tag, is mapped onto
  the OS3 Latin-1 charmap, including named and numeric entities
  that fit Latin-1.

* The default User-Agent is Firefox 4.0.1 on Windows 7. Some CDNs
  answer 403 when a Firefox-shaped agent also contains an Amiga
  token. The Spoof menu can still identify as Voyager.

* No vapor_toolkit.library and no keyfile required. All
  functionality is now unlocked.

* PNG alpha masks no longer crash the blit.

* Wide tables finish layout instead of hanging or corrupting
  the page.

The per-version history for the limited 3.4/3.3 line and for
Voyager 3.2 and older (3.0.0 through 3.2) is in CHANGELOG.md
in the source tree. The 3.3.0-3.3.127 build log is Source/V.ReadMe:

  https://github.com/amigazen/Voyager/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md

Dead VaporWare URLs (v3.vapor.com, bugs.vapor.com, mailing lists) no
longer apply. Historical notes: https://zapek.com/software/voyager/


Support & Bug reporting
=======================

For 3.5.3, use GitHub or email. The VaporWare bug tracker and
mailing list are gone.

  https://github.com/amigazen/Voyager
  voyager@amigazen.com

JSERROR.LOG in the program drawer is still useful for JS
quirks when that preference is enabled.

